# Overtime — a night shift at the pizzeria, from the other side of the desk.
# Non-explicit. Written for the Aside engine.
#
# Themes: being kept for a purpose you didn't pick; performing an
# identity for an audience; what is left of a person when the audience
# goes home. The cast are people, not threats — the threat is the job.

title: Overtime
author: Roxanne
start: n1_start

# ============================================================
# NIGHT ONE — the chair, the hall, the curtain
# ============================================================

== n1_start ==
bg office_night
music fan_hum
The office has two doors, one fan, and no window.
The fan is the only thing in the building that doesn't want anything from you.
You have a name badge. The name on it is yours. The photograph is not.
-> n1_monty

== n1_monty ==
sfx door_open
show monty neutral at left
monty: New one.
monty: You're in her chair.

* "Who was she?" -> n1_whowas
* "I'll move, if you want it." -> n1_move
* Say nothing. -> n1_silence

== n1_whowas ==
~ aff_monty -1
monty: Doesn't matter.
monty (flat): She's gone and you're here. That's the whole story.
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_move ==
~ aff_monty +1
monty: It's a chair.
monty (tired): She'd have laughed at you for saying that.
~ asked_about_her true
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_silence ==
~ aff_monty +2
~ let_quiet_stand true
monty: ...
monty: Huh.
monty (quiet): Most of them fill the quiet. You didn't.
hide monty
-> n1_hall

== n1_hall ==
bg west_hall
music none
The west hall runs long and dark and smells faintly of birthday cake.
Somewhere behind you the fan keeps turning, and keeps not caring.
sfx footstep
roxanne: I heard the door.
show roxanne smirk at center
roxanne: You're not supposed to be back here.

* "Neither are you." -> n1_banter
* "I'm doing my rounds." -> n1_rounds
* "I know. I'll go." -> n1_retreat

== n1_banter ==
~ aff_roxy +2
roxanne (laughs): No. I'm not.
roxanne: But I've been here longer, so I win.
show roxanne warm at center
roxanne (warm): ...You're not scared of me.
roxanne: That's either brave or stupid and I haven't decided which.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove

== n1_rounds ==
~ aff_roxy +1
roxanne: Rounds. Sure.
roxanne (flat): You know what I do on my rounds? I check that you're still breathing.
roxanne: Nobody asks me to. There's just nothing else to do at three in the morning.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove

== n1_retreat ==
~ aff_roxy -1
roxanne: Good.
roxanne (cold): Keep walking.
hide roxanne
-> n1_cove_cold

== n1_cove ==
bg cove
music music_box
The curtain is drawn, and something behind it is being very still.
You get the feeling it has been practising.
freddy: Hm.
show freddy idle at right
freddy: You can hear me. That's further than most get.

* "I can hear you." -> n1_hear
* "Who are you?" -> n1_name
* "What is this place?" -> n1_place

== n1_hear ==
~ aff_freddy +2
~ listened +1
freddy: ...
freddy (warm): Then stay a minute.
freddy: That's all anybody has ever wanted, you know. A minute, and someone actually listening.
-> n1_offer

== n1_name ==
freddy: A longer answer than you have time for.
freddy (wry): Ask me again once you've done a week. You'll have earned it.
-> n1_offer

== n1_place ==
~ listened +1
freddy: A restaurant that closes at nine.
freddy: And then stays open. For us. Only for us.
freddy (wry): Nobody has ever explained what we're supposed to be doing in here.
-> n1_offer

== n1_offer ==
freddy: There's a song that plays when the power dies.
freddy: I don't choose it. I'm just the one standing there when it stops.
freddy: Chica's in the kitchen. She'd like you, probably.
freddy: She likes everyone. It's the only thing left that she's allowed to do.
hide freddy
-> n1_kitchen

== n1_kitchen ==
bg east_corner
music none
The east corner is colder than the rest of the building.
sfx pot_clank
chica: Oh!
show chica neutral at center
chica: You're the new one. Hello. Hi.
chica (bright): I'm Chica, I do the kitchen, I've done the kitchen for a long time.

* "It's nice to meet you, Chica." -> n1_chica_nice
* "Why are you still working?" -> n1_chica_why
* Just watch her. -> n1_chica_watch

== n1_chica_nice ==
~ aff_chica +2
chica: ...
chica (bright): Nice to meet me. Nice to *meet* me.
chica: I'll be thinking about that for hours now. That's not a complaint.
~ asked_about_her true
-> n1_end

== n1_chica_why ==
~ aff_chica +1
chica: Because the kitchen doesn't finish.
chica: I clean it, and then it's dirty again, and then I clean it.
chica (flat): It's the only way I know it's still night.
-> n1_end

== n1_chica_watch ==
~ aff_chica -1
~ let_quiet_stand true
chica: ...
chica (small): You're going to be one of the quiet ones.
chica: That's alright. I'm good at those.
-> n1_end

== n1_cove_cold ==
bg cove
The curtain stays shut. You don't knock, and it doesn't open.
You get the sense that this was a test, and that you failed it politely.
-> n1_end

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Dawn. What the night was worth depends on how you spent it.
# ------------------------------------------------------------

== n1_end ==
bg office_night
music none
The lights come up at six like nothing happened at all.
Everything in the building is exactly where it was.
-> n1_dawn_check

== n1_dawn_check ==
if listened >= 1 and aff_chica >= 2 -> n1_dawn_good
if aff_monty >= 2 or aff_roxy >= 2 -> n1_dawn_mixed
-> n1_dawn_flat

== n1_dawn_good ==
You learned a name and used it, which is more than the badge ever did.
The badge says you are employed here. After tonight, that's not quite the same word it was.
~ nights +1
-> n1_out

== n1_dawn_mixed ==
You got a laugh out of one of them and a silence out of another.
It's a start. It's the kind of start that costs somebody something.
~ nights +1
-> n1_out

== n1_dawn_flat ==
You did your rounds. You checked the doors. You left at six.
Nothing in this building will remember that you were here, and that is the job.
-> n1_out

== n1_out ==
You clock out.
The chair is still warm. It will be warm tomorrow, too, whoever sits in it.
-> END
